       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum daily dose for adults.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Daily total:** The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and most inpatients get 1,200\u20132,400 mg/day. At 6,400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury and cardiovascular events go up sharply. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possibilities:\n- 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 1,600 mg total per day, split into several doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you intended and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first, because that dose is outside labeled limits."
      }
